  <tr ID="problem-1">
    <td>Slower walking, knee pain on stairs and one near-fall in the past six months, found on the comprehensive geriatric assessment at intake: gait speed 0.78 m/s, Timed Up and Go 13.8 seconds, unable to hold a tandem stance for 10 seconds, grip 24 kg; cause under evaluation with a geriatric medicine consultation</td><td>resolved</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>R26.81</td><td>S — Synthetic presenting problem of normal aging found on a comprehensive geriatric assessment; superseded at the consultation, when knee osteoarthritis with reduced leg strength and balance was diagnosed.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-2">
    <td>Primary osteoarthritis of both knees, diagnosed clinically by the ACR criteria (knee pain, age over 50, morning stiffness under 30 minutes, crepitus, bony enlargement, no warmth), with reduced quadriceps strength and balance and an increased risk of falls; KOOS JR 62</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>M17.0</td><td>S — Synthetic modern diagnosis made at the consultation: a common, mild condition of aging chosen for a figure with no documented illness; not a claim about his real knees.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-3">
    <td>Potentially inappropriate over-the-counter medicines (Beers 2023): naproxen most days for about two years and diphenhydramine for sleep three or four nights a week; both stopped at intake</td><td>resolved</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>Z79.1</td><td>S — Synthetic medication history found on the deprescribing review.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-4">
