    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Primary osteoarthritis of both knees (M17.0)</content>. Pain 2 of 10 and KOOS JR 76; he reaches town without stopping, the goal he set. Clinical Frailty Scale 3 and FRAIL 0 of 5: no longer pre-frail. [S]<list><item>Tai chi and the home program; gel and acetaminophen as needed.</item><item>Review in six months.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Low bone mass (M85.89)</content>. No falls or fractures; vitamin D adequate. [S]<list><item>Vitamin D3 daily; DXA in about eighteen months.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Protocol monitoring: items the monitoring protocol calls for at this visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Measure</th><th>Interval</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Knee pain (0 to 10)</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>2 of 10</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Knee function (KOOS JR)</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>76</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Knee examination (range of movement, effusion, alignment, crepitus)</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Crepitus, no effusion; quadriceps 5 of 5</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Exercise and self-management (strength and balance program, tai chi)</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Tai chi twice a week; home exercises</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Gait speed, Timed Up and Go, 30-second chair stand and four-stage balance test</td><td>Yearly, or after any fall</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Gait speed 0.96 m/s; Timed Up and Go 10.9 seconds; 11 chair stands; tandem stance 10 seconds</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Grip strength</td><td>Yearly</td><td>Completed today</td><td>26 kg right, 24 kg left</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Frailty (Clinical Frailty Scale, FRAIL scale)</td><td>Yearly</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Clinical Frailty Scale 3; FRAIL 0 of 5</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Medication review (Beers 2023): no NSAID tablets, sedating antihistamines or other anticholinergic medicines; over-the-counter purchases</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Diclofenac gel, acetaminophen as needed and vitamin D3 only</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Topical diclofenac: skin and use</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>A few mornings a week</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>25-hydroxyvitamin D</td><td>At baseline, after repletion, then yearly</td><td>Up to date</td><td>33 ng/mL three months ago; next in a year</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Vaccination review</td><td>Yearly</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Second recombinant zoster dose and high-dose influenza vaccine today; COVID-19 vaccine at the pharmacy this month</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>What matters most (4Ms)</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Reaches town without stopping; still teaching two mornings a week; a portable medical order discussed</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Mentation: mood, memory and sleep (4Ms)</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Mood and sleep good; memory unchanged by his account</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Goal progress:</paragraph><list><item>Find out why he walks more slowly and nearly fell. Outcome by 2026-03-16: Knee osteoarthritis with reduced quadriceps strength and balance, and diphenhydramine at night; no neurologic, thyroid, B12 or blood pressure cause [S]</item><item>Walk into town and back for his teaching without stopping to rest, and climb his stairs safely. Outcome by 2026-09-28: Gait speed 0.78 to 0.96 m/s; Timed Up and Go 13.8 to 10.9 seconds; walks to town without stopping; no falls [S]</item><item>No medicine he does not need, and none on the Beers list. Outcome by 2026-04-27: Naproxen and diphenhydramine stopped; sleeping without a sleep aid; chose not to take a cold remedy with diphenhydramine [S]</item><item>Knee pain 3 of 10 or less on stairs. Outcome by 2026-06-29: 5 to 2 of 10 on exercise, topical diclofenac and acetaminophen as needed; KOOS JR 62 to 74 [S]</item><item>Bones and falls: vitamin D above 30 ng/mL and no falls. In progress; target 2027-03-02 [S]</item></list><paragraph>Immunizations given today: Recombinant zoster vaccine, second of two doses; Influenza vaccine, high-dose, trivalent, preservative-free, for this season [S]</paragraph><paragraph>Guideline basis: Age-Friendly Health Systems: the 4Ms (What Matters, Medication, Mentation, Mobility) (2026); American Geriatrics Society 2023 updated AGS Beers Criteria for potentially inappropriate medication use in older adults (2023); Updating STEADI for Primary Care: Recommendations From the American Geriatrics Society Workgroup (2025); Physical Frailty: ICFSR International Clinical Practice Guidelines for Identification and Management (2019); 2019 American College of Rheumatology/Arthritis Foundation Guideline for the Management of Osteoarthritis of the Hand, Hip, and Knee (2019); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, rheumatoid arthritis and osteoarthritis, and osteoporosis monographs (2026); Adult Immunization Schedule by Age (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Review in six months; annual wellness visit in June. The clinic for any fall. [S]</paragraph></text>

